WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
In 1999, a group of European
countries replaced their own

2
00:00:04.220 --> 00:00:06.980
currencies with one shared currency:

3
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:12.040
the euro. By 2026, 21 of the 27 countries

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.340
in the European Union were using it.

5
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:16.480
No more fees for changing money.

6
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.440
No more guessing what a
neighbour's currency will be worth.

7
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:21.490
Those are real gains.

8
00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:24.230
So why would a country
give up its own money,

9
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:26.780
and what does it lose by doing so?

10
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.680
In this mission, you'll test
what happens when a shock

11
00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:31.540
hits just one member.

12
00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.580
Then you'll check the conditions
economists use to judge

13
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.060
whether sharing a currency can work.

14
00:00:37.060 --> 00:00:39.870
Your mission: find out
what a country gains,

15
00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:40.910
and what it gives up,

16
00:00:40.910 --> 00:00:42.530
when it shares a currency.
